      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Swer">Swer</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-h"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.1"/><pb n="398" ed="#liebermann"/>On ælmihtiges Godes naman, ðu me behete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.2"/> hal ⁊ clæne þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ðu me sealdest, ⁊ fulle ware wið æfterspræce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.3"/>, on ða gewitennesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.4-2"/>, ðe unc ða mid wæs: N.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.1-2"/><pb n="398" ed="#liebermann"/>Að gif man afindeð his æhte, syððan he hit geboht hafeð, unhal. On ealmihtiges Godes naman, ðu me behete hal ⁊ clæne þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi>, ðæt ðu me sealdest, ⁊ fulle ware wið æfterspræce, on ða gewitnesse, ðe unc ða mid wæs: N.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="399" ed="#liebermann"/>Per<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.4"/> omnipotentis Dei nomen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.5"/>, tu mihi promisisti sanum et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.6"/> mundum, quod mihi uendidisti, et plenam defensionem contra omnem postlocutionem, in eo testimonio, quod tunc nobiscum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Swer_7.lnote.oe.7"/> affuit, N.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="399" ed="#liebermann"/>(Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Swer_7.lnote.de.1"/> [des Klägers], wenn jemand sein<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Swer_7.lnote.de.2"/> Werthstück, nachdem er es gekauft hat, als fehlbehaftet erkennt. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>). Im Namen des allmächtigen Gottes, du<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Swer_7.lnote.de.3"/> hast mir das, was du mir verkauftest, heil<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Swer_7.lnote.de.4"/> und [von Anfechtung] rein versprochen und volle Gewähr gegen [dessen] zukünftige Einklagung, unter der Zeugenschaft, die da [beim Kaufe] bei uns beiden war: N.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(The oath [of the plaintiff] when someone, after buying his goods, finds them faulty. B) In the name of almighty God, you promised me that what you sold me was sound and clean [of any claim], and full warranty against any future claim [on it], in the witness that was then with us both [at the sale]: N.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-h">[I swear] in the name of Almighty God [that] you vowed that [the sale] was honest and true, and what you sold me was proof against future claims as was witnessed [by another] in our presence: N.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="399"><ref target="clause:Ine_56">Ine 56</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. Ine 56</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="421"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_56">Ine 56</ref> <quote>Compare to Hloþhere and Eadric §11 [L16]; see also Swerian §7 and §9. Æthelberht §76 [L77–81] similarly invokes the principle of unblemished goods</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">U: translator unrecorded: check; Liebermann compares Ine 56. K: a stray space before a comma removed.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">399</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">er <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">er Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">399</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ego <hi rend="italic">fügt zu R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ego added by R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">399</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et—nesciui <hi rend="italic">in c.</hi> 9 <hi rend="italic">überspringen MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et—nesciui in c. 9 skipped by MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">399</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nobis <hi rend="italic">T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nobis T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">398</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Platz für Überschrift frei</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Space left free for a heading</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">398</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> hete</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from hete</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">398</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> -spæce</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from -spæce</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">398</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">398</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Überschrift roth</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Heading in red</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hierauf antwortet 9.—<hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Handel 13—e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This is answered by 9.—<hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Handel 13—e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘am Gute Fehler’ grammatisch ungenau Schmid; <hi rend="italic">æhte</hi> ist ac. wie 3, 4 no. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. onfinde unhælo</hi>; Ine 56</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Schmid’s ‘defects in the goods’ is grammatically inaccurate; <hi rend="italic">æhte</hi> is acc., as it is nom. in 3, 4. <hi rend="italic">Cf. onfinde unhælo</hi>; Ine 56</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Wechselrede; <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Becwæð 3; Brunner II 342; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Rechtsgang 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Dialogue; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Becwæð 3; Brunner II 342; <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Rechtsgang 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Swer_7.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">235</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. u</hi>. 9; Fränkisch <hi rend="italic">sanum</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See below</hi> 9; Frankish <hi rend="italic">sanum</hi></seg></note>
      </div>
